          "text": "While Voltbuilder offers a streamlined process for building and deploying apps, it doesn't provide built-in continuous integration capabilities. If you're looking to implement a CI/CD pipeline alongside live updates, you might consider combining Capgo with a service like GitHub Actions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 37,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 37,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "GitHub Actions is a free, built-in continuous integration and deployment service for GitHub repositories. By setting up a workflow with GitHub Actions and integrating Capgo for live updates, you can create a powerful, automated development pipeline."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 39,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 39,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "To set this up, you would first create a GitHub repository for your app's code. Then, you can create a workflow file that defines the steps to be run whenever code is pushed to the repository. These steps might include building and testing the app, and then using Capgo to create and deploy a live update."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 41,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 41,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "This setup allows you to automatically build, test, and deploy your app with minimal effort, while still taking advantage of the live update capabilities offered by Capgo. For detailed instructions on setting up CI/CD with Capgo, you can refer to our tutorials for "
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "location": {
            "line": 41,
            "column": 266
          },
          "url": "https://capgo.app/blog/automatic-capacitor-android-build-github-action/",
          "title": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 41,
                "column": 267
              },
              "text": "iOS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 41,
            "column": 344
          },
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 43,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 43,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Let's go further"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 45,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 45,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "While Voltbuilder offers a straightforward solution for converting web projects into native apps, it may not be the best fit for all developers, especially those who prioritize live update capabilities and open-source solutions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 47,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 47,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Capgo has matured into a robust platform suitable for teams of all sizes, offering a more affordable solution with a focus on live updates. If you're a larger team requiring dedicated support, don't hesitate to reach out - we're always ready to find tailored solutions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 49,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 49,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Even though Capgo is designed to be self-service, we pride ourselves on being highly responsive to our users' needs. We can assist you with configuring your build for native code, eliminating the need for more expensive solutions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 51,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 51,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "If you appreciate open-source, self-service, community-driven tools, Capgo might be the perfect fit for your project."
        }
      ]
    },
